1. Permission
Subject to these terms, you may use, copy and modify MAP for your own personal
or business operations. You may self-host MAP and make backup copies. MAP
automates media-server account administration; it does not include member billing.

2. No resale
You may not sell, sublicense for a fee, or otherwise charge for copies of MAP
or derivative versions of MAP without the copyright holder's separate written
permission. This includes rebranded versions and bundling MAP into a paid software
product where payment buys rights to MAP. Separately charging for installation
or support does not itself constitute resale, provided you do not sell software
rights you have not been granted.

3. Member allowance and subscription
The GitHub-distributed application provides a free allowance of ten members.
Using the application above this allowance requires an active MAP unlock
subscription, priced at GBP 5 per month at the time these terms were published.
Administrators remain able to manage the installation and retained account
information. Failed payment or the end of the subscription returns the app to
its free allowance; it does not authorise deletion of stored account information.
The application checks its entitlement with the licensing service. A subscription permits up to three registered applications. Do not forge codes,
share them outside your licensed registrations, or circumvent activation or member
limits. Removing a registration disables that application while retaining its data.
Changes to price or subscription terms require separate notice and any consent
required by applicable law; this document does not itself change existing charges.

